-- title:
--   Primed chart ring as a base change: R'/πⁿ⁺¹≅ (R⊗_A A')/πⁿ⁺¹
-- statement:
--   Throughout, write $A :=$ `FixedPoints.subalgebra 𝒪 R G` for the $𝒪$-subalgebra of $G$-invariants of $R$, and for a ring $T$ receiving $\pi$ write $\bar{\ }$ for the reduction modulo the relevant power of (the image of) $\pi$.
--
--   **The unprimed tower.** $𝒪$ is a commutative domain, $hdvr$ asserts that it is a discrete valuation ring, $\pi\in𝒪$ is irreducible, and $hcomplete$ asserts that $𝒪$ is adically complete for $(\pi)$. A family of schemes $X_n$ ($n\in\mathbb N$) is given together with structure morphisms $xb_n : X_n\to\operatorname{Spec}(𝒪/(\pi^{n+1}))$ and transition morphisms $xt_n : X_n\to X_{n+1}$. The hypotheses on this tower are: $hcart$, that each square formed by $xt_n$, $xb_n$, $xb_{n+1}$ and the morphism of bases induced by the quotient map $𝒪/(\pi^{n+2})\to𝒪/(\pi^{n+1})$ is cartesian; $hproper$ and $hflat$, that every $xb_n$ is proper and flat; and $haff$, that in each $X_n$ every finite subset is contained in an affine open. A finite group $G$ is given with homomorphisms $a_n : G\to\operatorname{Aut}(X_n)$ such that $ha\_over$: each $a_n(g)$ commutes with $xb_n$ (i.e. acts over the base), and $ha\_xt$: the actions are compatible with the transitions, $a_n(g)$ followed by $xt_n$ equals $xt_n$ followed by $a_{n+1}(g)$.
--
--   **The quotient datum.** $D$ is a term of `TowerQuotientDatum 𝒪 π X xb xt G a`: it provides schemes $D.Y_n$ with structure morphisms $D.yb_n : D.Y_n\to\operatorname{Spec}(𝒪/(\pi^{n+1}))$ and transitions $D.yt_n$ whose squares over the bases are cartesian, with every $D.yb_n$ proper and flat, together with morphisms $D.p_n : X_n\to D.Y_n$ satisfying $D.p_n$ followed by $D.yb_n$ equals $xb_n$, the compatibility $xt_n$ followed by $D.p_{n+1}$ equals $D.p_n$ followed by $D.yt_n$, cartesianness of the square formed by $xt_n$, $D.p_n$, $D.p_{n+1}$, $D.yt_n$, invariance $a_n(g)$ followed by $D.p_n$ equals $D.p_n$, finiteness and surjectivity of each $D.p_n$, epimorphy of each restriction $D.p_n|_U$ over an open $U\subseteq D.Y_n$, and a local universal property `univ_loc` which, for a scheme $T$, a family of opens $U_n\subseteq D.Y_n$ with $D.yt_n^{-1}(U_{n+1})=U_n$ and morphisms $u_n : D.p_n^{-1}(U_n)\to T$ invariant under the restricted $G$-action, imposes the further clauses recorded in that field (summarised here).
--
--   **The primed tower over $S$.** $S$ is a commutative flat $𝒪$-algebra; schemes $X'_n$ are given with structure morphisms $xb'_n : X'_n\to\operatorname{Spec}(S/(\pi_S^{n+1}))$, where $\pi_S$ denotes the image of $\pi$ in $S$, transitions $xt'_n$, homomorphisms $a'_n : G\to\operatorname{Aut}(X'_n)$, and morphisms $q_n : X'_n\to X_n$. The hypotheses are: $hq$, that each square formed by $q_n$, $xb'_n$, $xb_n$ and the morphism of bases induced by $𝒪/(\pi^{n+1})\to S/(\pi_S^{n+1})$ is cartesian; $hcart'$, cartesianness of the transition squares over the bases $S/(\pi_S^{n+2})\to S/(\pi_S^{n+1})$; $hq\_xt$, that $xt'_n$ followed by $q_{n+1}$ equals $q_n$ followed by $xt_n$; $hq\_a$, that $a'_n(g)$ followed by $q_n$ equals $q_n$ followed by $a_n(g)$; and $ha'\_over$, that each $a'_n(g)$ acts over $\operatorname{Spec}(S/(\pi_S^{n+1}))$.
--
--   **The primed quotient tower and the opens $V_n$.** Schemes $Y'_n$ are given with $yb'_n : Y'_n\to\operatorname{Spec}(S/(\pi_S^{n+1}))$, transitions $yt'_n$, morphisms $p'_n : X'_n\to Y'_n$ and $r_n : Y'_n\to D.Y_n$, subject to: $hbase$, cartesianness of the square formed by $r_n$, $yb'_n$, $D.yb_n$ and the base-change morphism of bases; $hsq$, cartesianness of the square formed by $q_n$, $p'_n$, $D.p_n$, $r_n$ (so $X'_n = X_n\times_{D.Y_n} Y'_n$); $hyt'r$, $yt'_n$ followed by $r_{n+1}$ equals $r_n$ followed by $D.yt_n$; $hyt'b$, $yt'_n$ followed by $yb'_{n+1}$ equals $yb'_n$ followed by the base morphism; $hp'\_over$, $p'_n$ followed by $yb'_n$ equals $xb'_n$; $hp'\_inv$, $a'_n(g)$ followed by $p'_n$ equals $p'_n$; and $hp'\_xt$, $xt'_n$ followed by $p'_{n+1}$ equals $p'_n$ followed by $yt'_n$. Opens $V_n\subseteq D.Y_n$ are given with $hVa$: each $V_n$ affine, and $hV$: $D.yt_n^{-1}(V_{n+1})=V_n$.
--
--   **The unprimed chart rings.** $R$ is a commutative $𝒪$-algebra carrying a $G$-action by ring automorphisms commuting with the $𝒪$-action, with $hRc$: $R$ adically complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$; $hRtf$: the image of $\pi$ is not a zero divisor in $R$; $hRft$: $R/(\pi)$ is of finite type over $𝒪$. Ring isomorphisms $lvl_n : R/(\pi^{n+1})\;\xrightarrow{\sim}\;\Gamma(X_n, D.p_n^{-1}(V_n))$ and $\mu_n : A/(\pi^{n+1})\;\xrightarrow{\sim}\;\Gamma(D.Y_n, V_n)$ are given, compatible as follows: $hlvl\_xt$, the restriction along $xt_n$ from $D.p_{n+1}^{-1}(V_{n+1})$ to $D.p_n^{-1}(V_n)$ carries $lvl_{n+1}(\bar x)$ to $lvl_n(\bar x)$ for $x\in R$; $hlvl\_smul$, the action of $a_n(g^{-1})$ on sections over $D.p_n^{-1}(V_n)$ carries $lvl_n(\bar x)$ to $lvl_n(\overline{g\cdot x})$; $hlvl\_xb$, $lvl_n$ of the class of the image of $o\in𝒪$ in $R$ equals the pullback along $xb_n$ of the global section of $\operatorname{Spec}(𝒪/(\pi^{n+1}))$ corresponding to $\bar o$; $h\mu\_yt$, restriction along $D.yt_n$ from $V_{n+1}$ to $V_n$ carries $\mu_{n+1}(\bar x)$ to $\mu_n(\bar x)$ for $x\in A$; $h\mu\_p$, the pullback along $D.p_n$ from $V_n$ to $D.p_n^{-1}(V_n)$ carries $\mu_n(\bar x)$ to $lvl_n(\bar x)$, $x\in A$ regarded in $R$; $h\mu\_yb$, $\mu_n$ of the class of the image of $o\in𝒪$ in $A$ equals the pullback along $D.yb_n$ of the global section corresponding to $\bar o$.
--
--   **The element $b$ and the maps $\varphi_n$.** An element $b\in A\otimes_𝒪 S$ is given, together with additive maps $\varphi_n : A\otimes_𝒪 S\to\Gamma(Y'_n, r_n^{-1}(V_n))$ satisfying $h\varphi$: on a pure tensor, $\varphi_n(x\otimes s)$ is the product of the pullback along $r_n$ of $\mu_n(\bar x)$ with the pullback along $yb'_n$ of the global section of $\operatorname{Spec}(S/(\pi_S^{n+1}))$ corresponding to $\bar s$; $h\varphi s$: each $\varphi_n$ is surjective; and $hV'$: $yt'^{-1}_n\bigl(D(\varphi_{n+1}(b))\bigr) = D(\varphi_n(b))$, where $D(\cdot)$ denotes the basic open in $Y'_n$ attached to a section.
--
--   **The primed chart ring.** $R'$ is a commutative $S$-algebra with a $G$-action by ring automorphisms commuting with the $S$-action, with $hR'c$: $R'$ adically complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi_S$, and $hR'tf$: that image is not a zero divisor. Ring isomorphisms $lvl'_n : R'/(\pi_{R'}^{n+1})\;\xrightarrow{\sim}\;\Gamma\bigl(X'_n, p'^{-1}_n(D(\varphi_n(b)))\bigr)$ are given ($\pi_{R'}$ the image of $\pi_S$ in $R'$), satisfying the three compatibilities $hlvl'\_xt$ (restriction along $xt'_n$ carries $lvl'_{n+1}(\bar x)$ to $lvl'_n(\bar x)$), $hlvl'\_smul$ (the action of $a'_n(g^{-1})$ carries $lvl'_n(\bar x)$ to $lvl'_n(\overline{g\cdot x})$) and $hlvl'\_xb$ ($lvl'_n$ of the class of the image of $s\in S$ equals the pullback along $xb'_n$ of the global section corresponding to $\bar s$).
--
--   **The localisation $A'$ and the identifications $\beta_n,\theta_n$.** $A'$ is a commutative $(A\otimes_𝒪 S)$-algebra which is a localisation of $A\otimes_𝒪 S$ away from $b$, and also an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A\to A\otimes_𝒪 S\to A'$. Ring isomorphisms $\beta_n : (A\otimes_𝒪 S)/(\pi^{n+1})\;\xrightarrow{\sim}\;\Gamma(Y'_n, r_n^{-1}(V_n))$ are given with $h\beta$: $\beta_n(\bar z)=\varphi_n(z)$; and ring isomorphisms $\theta_n : A'/(\iota(\pi_S)^{n+1})\;\xrightarrow{\sim}\;\Gamma\bigl(Y'_n, D(\varphi_n(b))\bigr)$, where $\iota$ is the composite $S\to A\otimes_𝒪 S\to A'$, with $h\theta$: for $z\in A\otimes_𝒪 S$, $\theta_n$ of the class of the image of $z$ in $A'$ equals the restriction of $\varphi_n(z)$ from $r_n^{-1}(V_n)$ to the basic open $D(\varphi_n(b))$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exists a family of ring isomorphisms
--   $$\tau_n : \bigl(R\otimes_{A} A'\bigr)\big/\bigl(\pi_R^{n+1}\otimes 1\bigr)\;\xrightarrow{\sim}\;R'/(\pi_{R'}^{n+1}),$$
--   the source being the quotient by the ideal generated by the single element $(\pi_R^{n+1})\otimes 1$ with $\pi_R$ the image of $\pi$ in $R$, such that all of the following hold.
--
--   (i) Compatibility with the transitions: for every $n$, every $z\in R\otimes_A A'$ and every $y\in R'$, if $\tau_{n+1}(\bar z)=\bar y$ then $\tau_n(\bar z)=\bar y$.
--
--   (ii) $G$-equivariance on pure tensors: for every $n$, $g\in G$, $x\in R$, $w\in A'$ and $y\in R'$, if $\tau_n(\overline{x\otimes w})=\bar y$ then $\tau_n(\overline{(g\cdot x)\otimes w})=\overline{g\cdot y}$.
--
--   (iii) Compatibility with $S$: for every $n$ and every $s\in S$, $\tau_n\bigl(\overline{1\otimes\iota(s)}\bigr)$ is the class of the image of $s$ in $R'$, where $\iota$ is the composite $S\to A\otimes_𝒪 S\to A'$.
--
--   (iv) Compatibility with $\theta_n$ and $lvl'_n$: for every $n$, $w\in A'$ and $y\in R'$, if $\tau_n\bigl(\overline{1\otimes w}\bigr)=\bar y$, then the pullback along $p'_n$ from $D(\varphi_n(b))$ to $p'^{-1}_n(D(\varphi_n(b)))$ of $\theta_n(\bar w)$ equals $lvl'_n(\bar y)$.
--
--   This identifies the chart ring of the base-changed tower as a base change and localisation of the chart ring of the original tower: $R'/\pi^{n+1}$ is recovered from $\bigl(R\otimes_{R^G}(R^G\otimes_𝒪 S)[1/b]\bigr)/\pi^{n+1}$, compatibly with the transition maps, the $G$-action, the $S$-algebra structure and the identifications of sections over the basic open $D(\varphi_n(b))$. It is used in the construction of the flat base change of a tower quotient datum, in [`AlgebraicGeometry.TowerQuotientDatum.exists_flat_ringEquiv_tensorProduct_quotient_and_sections_basicOpen`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.TowerQuotientDatum.exists_flat_ringEquiv_tensorProduct_quotient_and_sections_basicOpen).
